1
00:00:02,710 --> 00:00:06,980
My new book The Hidden Reality
takes on a grand question:

2
00:00:06,990 --> 00:00:09,950
(Dr. Brian Greene:)Is our universe
the only universe?

3
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:13,190
(Dr. Brian Greene:)You see, there's a growing
belief among scientists like me

4
00:00:13,190 --> 00:00:16,760
(Dr. Brian Greene:)that ours may only be one
among many universes

5
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:18,830
(Dr. Brian Greene:)populating a gigantic cosmos.

6
00:00:18,830 --> 00:00:21,770
In The Hidden Reality,
I explore this possibility

7
00:00:21,770 --> 00:00:24,700
(Dr. Brian Greene:)without presuming any knowledge
of mathematics or physics

8
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:25,900
(Dr. Brian Greene:)on the part of the reader.

9
00:00:25,910 --> 00:00:29,210
(Sheldon:)Hysterical.

10
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:31,680
(Amy:)I'm glad you
talked me into this.

11
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:34,150
(Amy:)We work so hard, sometimes,
it's nice to goof off

12
00:00:34,150 --> 00:00:36,850
(Amy:)and do something silly.
Agreed.

13
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:40,380
(Sheldon:)Wait till you hear how he dumbs down
Werner Heisenberg for the crowd.

14
00:00:40,390 --> 00:00:42,400
(Sheldon:)You may actually believe
you're in a comedy club.

15
00:00:42,410 --> 00:00:46,520
(Greene:)You can think about Heisenberg's
"uncertainty principle"

16
00:00:46,530 --> 00:00:48,530
(Greene:)much like the special order menu

17
00:00:48,530 --> 00:00:50,960
(Greene:)that you find in certain Chinese
restaurants, where you have

18
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:54,000
(Greene:)dishes in column A
and other dishes in column B,

19
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,130
(Greene:)and if you order the first dish
in column A,

20
00:00:56,140 --> 00:00:58,340
(Greene:)you can't order the
corresponding dish in column B.

21
00:00:58,340 --> 00:01:00,910
(Greene:)That's sort of like the
"uncertainly principle."

22
00:01:00,910 --> 00:01:04,110
♪ Ba-dum-bump. ♪

